{
  "instructions": "BuzzSearch researches what real people say in Reddit, YouTube, TikTok and Facebook group comments and returns verbatim quotes with source links. Use it for customer pains, desires, objections, product feedback, audience language and ad angles.\n\nWhat `search` accepts: a research question; a TikTok video, profile or hashtag link, a creator @handle, a YouTube video or channel link, a Reddit thread or subreddit link, or a Facebook group post link (reads that link's comments; add a question after it to also search the topic); or a pasted list of comments (analyzed directly). Options: depth quick (default), deep or exhaustive; sources; time_range for recent posts only.\n\nWorkflow: call list_searches first and reuse a completed search on the same topic. Otherwise call search. A search takes one to three minutes: when it returns before completion, call get_search with the given search_id and turn_id until status is completed, then answer.\n\nAfter a search completes, none of these search again: get_quotes (verbatim quotes filtered by dimension, source, intensity or text), get_sources (threads and videos read), get_comments (raw comment bodies), ask (a follow-up question over the same corpus), generate_hooks (ad hooks grounded in the quotes).\n\nQuote customers verbatim and cite each quote's url. When a reply includes sources_url, give it to the user: it opens every comment and source the search read, searchable and filterable.",
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "search",
      "title": "Search UGC and social comments across the web",
      "description": "Search the web for user-generated content: what real people say about a product, problem or audience in comments on Reddit, YouTube, TikTok and Facebook groups. Runs a full live search: finds threads and videos across the web, reads their comments, extracts verbatim quotes and writes a cited answer. A query that contains a TikTok video, creator profile or hashtag link, a bare creator @handle (TikTok unless the query says YouTube), a YouTube video or channel link, a Reddit thread or subreddit link, or a Facebook group post link reads that link's own comments directly (add a question after the link to also search the topic). A query that is a pasted list of comments is analyzed directly with no web search. A search usually takes one to three minutes, longer than one call can wait: it waits up to `wait_seconds` and returns the answer with the top quotes when done, otherwise the exact `get_search` call to make next; keep calling `get_search` until the status is completed. Costs credits from the BuzzSearch balance at the API rate; the exact charge is reported on completion as `credits_charged` with `balance_after`. When the balance cannot cover a search the call fails with INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS and a top-up link: tell the user and share the link. Check `list_searches` first: a prior search on the same topic can be reread for free.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "query": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 3,
            "maxLength": 2000,
            "description": "The research question, e.g. 'what do people hate about robot vacuums'."
          },
          "depth": {
            "default": "quick",
            "description": "quick (about a minute), deep (about three), exhaustive (longest, most comments).",
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "quick",
              "deep",
              "exhaustive"
            ]
          },
          "sources": {
            "description": "Default: reddit, youtube, tiktok. Add facebook for group discussions.",
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "reddit",
                "youtube",
                "tiktok",
                "facebook"
              ]
            }
          },
          "time_range": {
            "description": "How recent the posts and comments should be. Default: any time.",
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "past_week",
              "past_month",
              "past_3_months",
              "past_6_months",
              "past_year"
            ]
          },
          "wait_seconds": {
            "default": 45,
            "description": "Seconds to wait server-side for completion before returning (0 to 55). Call again to resume.",
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0,
            "maximum": 55
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "query"
        ],
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
      },
      "annotations": {
        "title": "Search UGC and social comments across the web",
        "readOnlyHint": false,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": false,
        "openWorldHint": true
      },
      "execution": {
        "taskSupport": "forbidden"
      },
      "_meta": {
        "ui": {
          "resourceUri": "ui://buzzsearch/search-card-v2.html"
        },
        "openai/outputTemplate": "ui://buzzsearch/search-card-v2.html",
        "openai/toolInvocation/invoking": "Searching comments",
        "openai/toolInvocation/invoked": "Search started"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "get_search",
      "title": "Get a search",
      "description": "Read a search's status, cited answer, coverage counts and top quotes. Free. Pass `turn_id` to read a specific follow-up answer, otherwise the latest turn is returned. A finished search returns at once; a running one is held open for up to 55s and returns as soon as it finishes, so call it again until status is \"completed\".",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "search_id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The search id returned by `search` or `list_searches`."
          },
          "turn_id": {
            "description": "A turn id from `search`, `ask` or `generate_hooks`. Default: the latest turn.",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "search_id"
        ],
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
      },
      "annotations": {
        "title": "Get a search",
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false
      },
      "execution": {
        "taskSupport": "forbidden"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "get_quotes",
      "title": "Get quotes",
      "description": "Verbatim customer quotes extracted by a search, filtered and paged. Free. Each quote carries a stable id, the source url, a dimension (emotional_painpoints, recurring_painpoints, desired_outcomes, failed_solutions, objections, customer_lingo), an engagement score and an emotional intensity (1 to 5). For ad copy, pull emotional_painpoints and customer_lingo sorted by intensity.",
      "inputSchema": {
